  "id": "COMPOUND:28227 - PROTEIN:5817",
  "verbalization": "Tamulamide B is associated with HepG2 through a series of molecular pathways, all of which ultimately point to the same target, MIP. The evidence suggests that Tamulamide B interacts with MIP, which is then targeted by multiple structurally diverse compounds, including the compound (1S,3R,6S,8R,11S,12S,15R,16R)-15-[(2R)-4-[(2R)-3,3-dimethyloxiran-2-yl]butan-2-yl]-7,7,12,16-tetramethylpentacyclo[9.7.0.01,3.03,8.012,16]octadecan-6-ol, and another compound with a similar structure, (4S,5S)-5-[(1R,2R)-2-Hydroxy-2-Methyl-5-Oxocyclopent-3-En-1-Yl]-3-Methylidene-4-(3-Oxobutyl)Oxolan-2-One. These compounds all share a common target, HepG2, indicating a potential mechanism of action involving MIP. The evidence suggests that Tamulamide B may act through a similar mechanism, targeting MIP and thereby influencing HepG2. The recurring involvement of MIP and HepG2 in multiple pathways supports the hypothesis that Tamulamide B interacts with HepG2 via MIP, though the exact molecular mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
